{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1205269-scarred-lands-community-content-frequently-asked-questions","id":1205269,"title":"Scarred Lands Community Content Frequently Asked Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scarred Lands"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-10T10:04:36-07:00","id":1205269,"title":"Scarred Lands Community Content Frequently Asked Questions","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Frequently Asked Questions</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Ownership and License Questions</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Slacecian Vault is not an open game license. Beyond what is allowable with the OGL, content creators only have permission to use those unique game systems and background materials explicitly permitted by Slacecian Vault. Content creators are not allowed to use other material for original content unless they have a license to do so from Onyx Path Publishing (which requires a separate agreement).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If you\u2019re still not sure about what you are allowed to publish, check the table below to see if that helps.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Allowed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I want to\u2026</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">design content using the </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Scarred Lands</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> rules for </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Scarred Lands</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">-related content</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">have my content considered for additional publication by Onyx Path</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">have my content considered for inclusion in digital games</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">have my content considered for inclusion in </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Scarred Lands</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> marketing</span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Not Allowed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I cannot\u2026</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">publish my original IP using non-OGL elements of the </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Scarred Lands</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> rules</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">print and sell my </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Scarred Lands</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> products on my own</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">publish content set outside of Gelspad at this time</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">publish crossover games with IPs that do not belong to Onyx Path</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">publish my own rules system for games set in the </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Scarred Lands</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> world</span></li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Does Onyx Path own the content that I create in my Slacecian Vault publications?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Yes. Further, content creators are not allowed to create new intellectual property under the Slacecian Vault program. Rather, every piece of content created uses the Onyx Path IP. That said, if your work merits incorporation into canon, Onyx Path will contact you.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Slacecian Vault agreement will grant other Slacecian Vault authors a license to use your original content at any time from its publication date. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">What do I include in the legal text within my Slacecian Vault title?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">We recommend a legal section in this general format:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>This product was created under license. SCARRED LANDS and its logo, and SLACECIAN VAULT and its logo, are trademarks of Onyx Path Publishing. All Scarred Lands setting material, art, and trade dress are the property of Onyx Path Publishing. <a href=\"https://www.theonyxpath.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.theonyxpath.com</a></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>This work contains material that is copyright Onyx Path Publishing. Such material is used with permission under the Community Content Agreement for \u201cSlacecian Vault\u201d Community Content. All other original material in this work is copyright [THIS YEAR] by [YOUR LEGAL NAME OR COMPANY NAME] and published under the Community Content Agreement for \u201cSlacecian Vault\u201d Community Content.</i></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If I use content from other Slacecian Vault authors, do I need to credit them?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">As more authors contribute to the Slacecian Vault\u2019s pool of community content, we do not expect to maintain perfect attribution every time some author re-uses elements originally contributed by another author. Such attributions are not strictly required. However, we do think two things would be best practices for all Slacecian Vault contributors:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">When re-using a larger element that you have taken from another Slacecian Vault author\u2019s work, include a reference to the original work as a link to the DriveThruRPG page within your PDF. For example, if you use a new enemy called the Slitherin Mystics that you found in another author\u2019s work, you should reference that inside your own work using an internal citation such as &quot;Slitherin Mystics from </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Sharper Than A Serpent\u2019s Tooth</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> by Jane Doe&quot;.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">On your title\u2019s credit page, make a list of such references.</span></li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Content and Format Questions</span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">What can I use in my products on the Slacecian Vault?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">When you create your own title for the Slacecian Vault, you get access to a hoard of resources. Your work can use any of the rules published by Onyx Path. Additionally, Onyx Path and OneBookShelf will from time to time make additional resources such as stock art, template cover designs, and other such assets available for you to freely use in your Slacecian Vault titles.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">As others create content for the Slacecian Vault and expand the world through their titles, you then have access to use that material in turn. All Slacecian Vault creators contribute to a pool of community content that can be re-used, expanded, and explored by other creators in the Slacecian Vault community.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">In short, this is an opportunity to take part in a massive communal design network, one that is officially recognized and sanctioned by Onyx Path.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I don\u2019t see anything that would stop me from publishing products set outside Gelspad on Slacecian Vault. Can I do that?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Not at this time. In the near future, we will announce and update the Content Guidelines as new game settings become available on the Slacecian Vault. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Can I publish comic books, computer games, apps, and so on on Slacecian Vault?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">No. For now, we ask that you publish RPG supplements, fiction, and stock art illustrations only, please. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Can I sell my Slacecian Vault title in print as well as PDF?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">No. At this time, we are not allowing new print files for Community Content programs. If you have questions about this, contact publisher services at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#6c1c190e00051f04091e1f091e1a050f091f2c0302090e0303071f0409000a420f0301\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"c4b4b1a6a8adb7aca1b6b7a1b6b2ada7a1b784abaaa1a6ababafb7aca1a8a2eaa7aba9\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">How do I prepare the PDF of my title for sale?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">There are many different programs to lay out and prepare your book for digital download. Here are some things to help you make sure your PDF will download properly and look great!</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">CREATE - If you want to lay out your digital PDF from scratch</span></span><ul><li><a href=\"https://onebookshelfpublisherservice.zendesk.com/entries/94323298-Digital-Tutorials-and-Templates\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0563C1\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">TUTORIALS</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> - Tutorials for new publishers, to help you use Adobe Acrobat software to make better downloadable PDFs.</span></li> <li><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/site_resources/Digital_Specs%20201506.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0563C1\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">QUICK SPECS (PDF)</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> - To get you started.</span></li> <li><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/site_resources/Digital_checklist%20201506.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0563C1\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">QUICK CHECK LIST (PDF)</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> - To be sure you don't miss anything.</span></li> <li><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/site_resources/HowToExportEPub-Mobi.pdf%20\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0563C1\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">EPUB &amp; MOBI EXPORT TUTORIAL - FROM INDESIGN (PDF)</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> - To show you how to prepare your InDesign file for export to the ePub format, and how to use Calibre to convert your ePub file to the mobi format.</span></li> <li><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/site_resources/HowToWORD-EPUB-Mobi.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0563C1\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">EPUB &amp; MOBI EXPORT TUTORIAL - FROM MICROSOFT WORD (PDF)</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> - To show you how to prepare your Microsoft Word file for export to the ePub format, and how to use Calibre to convert your ePub file to the mobi format.</span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">PREP - You've already created your PDF and just need to see if it is all set to upload</span></span><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/site_resources/Digital_Specs%20201506.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0563C1\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">QUICK SPECS (PDF)</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> - To get you started.</span></li> <li><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/site_resources/Digital_checklist%20201506.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0563C1\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">QUICK CHECK LIST (PDF)</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> - To be sure you don't miss anything.</span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">ENHANCE - You've already created your PDF and want to add enhancements</span></span><ul><li><a href=\"https://onebookshelfpublisherservice.zendesk.com/entries/94424318-Video-Tutorials\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0563C1\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">VIDEO TUTORIALS</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> - To enhance your PDF.</span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">READY - Once your files are ready to upload</span></span><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.onebookshelf.com/forward.php?forward_page=pub_upload_files.php\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0563C1\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">UPLOAD</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> - Will show you where and how to upload your files for digital download.</span></li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Fantasy Grounds, Roll20, and Virtual Tabletop Content</span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Can I publish Fantasy Grounds, Roll20, or other virtual tabletop compatible content through Slacecian Vault?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Yes! As long as your material follows the other posted guidelines, you can produce content for Fantasy Grounds, Roll20, and other virtual tabletop programs.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">What is Fantasy Grounds Content?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Fantasy Grounds is a virtual table top (VTT) program published by SmiteWorks that lets you play RPGs virtually with your friends. Now you can do that with Slacecian Vault content! This lets you play out your favorite community created adventures, monsters, heroes, and other user made enhancements to your game.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">How do I make a Fantasy Grounds file?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Most Fantasy Grounds content will be in the form of .mod files created by using the export features from Fantasy Grounds. More information is available in the Fantasy Grounds' Developer Guides: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">http://www.fantasygrounds.com/wiki/index.php/Developer_Guides</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">How do I upload my Fantasy Grounds compatible content?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">You upload your content nearly the same way as any other Slacecian Vault title. On your Account page, click on Enter New Community Created Title, just like you normally would. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">When you see the options for &quot;Publish Community Content&quot; or &quot;Publish Fantasy Grounds Content&quot; choose &quot;Publish Fantasy Grounds Content&quot;. This will note your product as Fantasy Grounds compatible, so we can display it in the right places on the marketplace.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">What if I already have a PDF of my title for sale? Can I make a Fantasy Grounds file for it?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Yes! But you should then republish the title so that you use the \u201cPublish Fantasy Grounds Content\u201d button per above for the new title listing. Then make private your old listing that was for the PDF-only version using the Edit Title link under My Content on your Account page.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">What logos can I use?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The normal artwork rules apply for the thumbnail image/covers, as can be seen here.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">For titles with Fantasy Grounds content, you can continue to use the Slacecian Vault logo, but to make it stand out, you can also use this Fantasy Grounds logo on your cover.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">How do I use these files?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">For help installing and using files on Fantasy Grounds, take a look at the Fantasy Grounds User Guides here:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">http://www.fantasygrounds.com/wiki/index.php/User_Guides</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Can I make a Fantasy Grounds version of another author's Slacecian Vault release?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The artwork, including cartography, that another author includes in their Slacecian Vault title does not become re-usable by other Slacecian Vault authors. For this reason, it's likely very challenging to make a Fantasy Grounds compatible version of another author's work without contacting that author and working with them on it as a co-published project. Authors can be contacted by leaving them a message in the Discussion thread of their product.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Logo and Artwork Questions</span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">What kinds of artwork and maps can I use in my Slacecian Vault products?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The artwork (such as illustrations and maps) that you include in your product becomes part of the Slacecian Vault content that other Slacecian Vault contributors can then use. Here is general advice for these types of artwork:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Art provided by Onyx Path</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">. The art you find in the Resources for Slacecian Vault Creators category is owned by Onyx Path and can be freely used in your Slacecian Vault titles. No other artwork from Onyx Path can be used \u2014 only the art specifically released for Slacecian Vault Creators.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Public Domain Art.</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Art that is in the public domain can be used, but it must be listed in the credits.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Stock Art. </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Usage of stock art depends on the license associated with that stock art. Most of the stock art sold under the Slacecian Vault Resources category on DriveThruRPG includes a license that would allow it to be used in your Slacecian Vault titles.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Commissioned Art.</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> You must have all the rights to the art in your project. Commissioned artwork may have not been previously used for any other IP that is not a part of the Slacecian Vault.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Creative Commons.</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> This depends on the type of Creative Commons license. Some allow commercial use, while others do not.</span></li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">What logos are required and allowed on my Slacecian Vault product?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">You are required to use the Slacecian Vault logo on the cover of any product. You may not use the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Scarred Lands</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> logo or any other game line logo as part of your RPG product title.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Do I have to use the templates provided by Onyx Path?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">You are highly recommended to use Onyx Path templates, but they are not a requirement.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Payment and Pricing Questions</span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">How should I price my product?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">When you upload your Slacecian Vault product, you will enter all the metadata for your product, including setting its price. You have the option to set the price to be free ($0). You can also set the price to be Pay What You Want (PWYW), meaning that each customer can set their own price (from $0 up) to pay for your product. Most products, though, will be priced at a fixed price.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The ideal fixed price varies with the length of RPG product and its quality of writing, art, and design. Based on historic data from DriveThruRPG sales for PDFs, the most successful price points are $1.00, $2.00, $2.95, $3.95, $4.99, $7.95, $10.00, $14.95, and $19.99.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">More detail can be found in this </span></span><a href=\"http://oneblogshelf.blogspot.com/2014/05/pricing-part-2.html\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0563C1\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">OneBookShelf</span></span></a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> blog post.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">How do I get paid?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Once you activate your Slacecian Vault title for public sale, your account will begin to accrue a 50% royalty every time your product sells. You can withdraw your accumulated royalties via PayPal by going to the My Money section of the Account page. Note that the My Money section of your Account page will not display until you have a balance accrued.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">There is a $2 fee to cover the cost of each withdrawal, but you will pay no other fees, either to us or to PayPal, to receive your money.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">To prevent certain types of fraud, we must hold back the amount of royalties you earned in the past 60 days from being eligible for withdrawal. The amount eligible for withdrawal at any time, is your total account earnings balance less the amount earned in the past 60 days. You may use your earnings as site credit to pay for orders on site; this will lower your earnings balance and the amount eligible for withdrawal.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">We pay royalties only via PayPal. Creating a PayPal account is free and easy, and in most countries, you can connect your PayPal account to your bank account and transfer money from PayPal to your bank in a few business days.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">DriveThruRPG Publisher Account Questions</span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I already have a publisher account at DriveThruRPG. Should I use my normal publisher tools for submitting Slacecian Vault products?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">No. Slacecian Vault products are managed from the My Content section of your Account page on DriveThruRPG.com. Do not use your normal Publisher Hub to set up new Slacecian Vault products. Royalties for Slacecian Vault product sales will likewise accrue in your customer account, not in your publisher earnings account </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Can I use my publisher tools on my Slacecian Vault content?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Slacecian Vault content is associated only with your customer account, not your publisher account. The tools available to you for your Slacecian Vault content are found on the Account page of Slacecian Vault. They are a simplified subset of your normal publisher tools.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Can I release the same products on both Slacecian Vault and as an independent publisher?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Any content created for the Slacecian Vault, which is completely separate from your other publishing efforts, must remain exclusive to Slacecian Vault. It cannot be listed anywhere else, and will not be considered part of your publisher account (though it will be part of your \u201cMy Content\u201d on the Slacecian Vault).</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Other Questions</span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Can I submit non-English language titles to the Slacecian Vault program?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Please do! You can submit your content in any language.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Can I submit translated material to the Slacecian Vault originally published by other creators?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Yes, you may translate Slacecian Vault content with the permission of the original content creator, which will require an agreement between the creator and the translator. This may result in a revenue sharing program as administered by DriveThruRPG.com.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Can I submit translated material of previously officially published Onyx Path products?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Not at this time. We are in the process of working with professional translation companies.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Will material be approved by Onyx Path before it is published on the Slacecian Vault?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">There will not be a formal approval process by Onyx Path or OneBookShelf, per se. However, if you\u2019re found to be breaking our content guidelines, there will be repercussions. For example, your content can be pulled from the site, you might be ejected from Slacecian Vault as a content creator, and you would receive no payment for copies sold.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Can anyone rate my Slacecian Vault content?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Only people who purchase your content are allowed to rate and review it. Anyone can join the Discussion on your product page, however.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">It is encouraged to keep reviews of other's work positive and helpful, in keeping with the community atmosphere.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Can I rate my Slacecian Vault content?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">No. Self-reviews are not allowed.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2F5496\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Can I become an administrator for the Slacecian Vault?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">At this time, all administration responsibilities are handled by OneBookShelf and Onyx Path staff.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:51:07-07:00","id":1205401,"title":"","content":"Yihaa! Thanks a lot for this FAQ and getting the Slarecian Vault started <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have plenty of (silly?) questions ^^<br /> <br /> - Do we need to include a copy of the OGL in the document?<br /> <br /> - Still related to licensing, the use of OGL seems to imply that we can publish for either/both 5E and Pathfinder. Can we publish for other OGL-based games? (such as D&amp;D 3.5 for example, or the upcoming Pathfinder 2nd edition when it will be launched, assuming it is still based on the OGL)<br /> <br /> - Can we convert old Scarred Lands OGL material (prestige classes, monsters, spells, magic items, etc) to newer versions of the game (such as 5E or Pathfinder)?<br /> <br /> - Is it possible to set a product in a different period (for example, play during the Divine War, or during the Ledean Empire period), or in an alternative present (for example, where the titans won the Divine War)?<br /> <br /> Finally, can we create...<br /> - new playable races? (I ask the question since if I recall correctly Canis Minor explicitly forbids it)<br /> - new playable classes?<br /> - new kingdoms or city-states?<br /> - new cities within existing kingdoms?<br /> - new factions? (such as guilds, mercenary companies, and the like)<br /> - new major gods/titans?<br /> - new minor gods/titans?<br /> - new dead gods? (come on, we know that the titans did not only kill Miridium and That Which Abideos XD<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Alain%20Giorla\" target=\"_blank\">Slarecian Vault contributions</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5793-haaz","name":"haaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T08:36:59-07:00","id":1206465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1205269-scarred-lands-community-content-frequently-asked-questions?p=1205401#post1205401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yihaa! Thanks a lot for this FAQ and getting the Slarecian Vault started <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have plenty of (silly?) questions ^^<br /> <br /> - Do we need to include a copy of the OGL in the document?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, we'll have that in the templates we're releasing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Still related to licensing, the use of OGL seems to imply that we can publish for either/both 5E and Pathfinder. Can we publish for other OGL-based games? (such as D&amp;D 3.5 for example, or the upcoming Pathfinder 2nd edition when it will be launched, assuming it is still based on the OGL) </div> </div> </div>Currently we're only unlocking Pathfiner and 5e OGL, since those are the current published books. We're exploring other options, but we won't have any of that at launch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Can we convert old Scarred Lands OGL material (prestige classes, monsters, spells, magic items, etc) to newer versions of the game (such as 5E or Pathfinder)? </div> </div> </div>The goal of the program is Create. Don't Copy. So, we're mostly interested in new material, especially adventures. So, if updating some of those things makes sense for the new material someone is creating (say you make an adventure that uses an old monster and you want to update that 3e monster to 5e). A straight up compilation of just old stuff to new system isn't actually creating anything, its just copying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Is it possible to set a product in a different period (for example, play during the Divine War, or during the Ledean Empire period), or in an alternative present (for example, where the titans won the Divine War)? </div> </div> </div>Not at this time. We're looking for supplements to the current books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, can we create...<br /> - new playable races? (I ask the question since if I recall correctly Canis Minor explicitly forbids it)<br /> - new playable classes?<br /> - new kingdoms or city-states?<br /> - new cities within existing kingdoms?<br /> - new factions? (such as guilds, mercenary companies, and the like)<br /> - new major gods/titans?<br /> - new minor gods/titans?<br /> - new dead gods? (come on, we know that the titans did not only kill Miridium and That Which Abideos XD </div> </div> </div>Sure, though we're not looking for people to &quot;convert&quot; existing OGL content and calling it &quot;new&quot; because it is set in Scarred Lands (hope that makes sense)<br /> <br /> -M","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T11:25:45-07:00","id":1206963,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot for these answers, they are very helpful to understand the goals and boundaries of the Slarecian Vault <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have a small question (more of a request actually) for the templates. I have looked at the one that are available for Canis Minor, and it seems they are all Photoshop templates. I am going to use different tools however (I don't have Photoshop, and I don't plan to get it), so do you think it would be possible to include in these template a PDF version of an example, so that we can produce something that looks like it without having to rely on Photoshop?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Alain%20Giorla\" target=\"_blank\">Slarecian Vault contributions</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5793-haaz","name":"haaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T16:06:17-07:00","id":1220645,"title":"","content":"I had a rather silly question about the OGL. For 5E documents, which source must we add in the Copyright Notice. OGL v 1.0a, SRD 5.1 and the PG itself must clearly be there, but I'm not sure about the previous 3E books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Alain%20Giorla\" target=\"_blank\">Slarecian Vault contributions</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5793-haaz","name":"haaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T16:47:21-07:00","id":1320028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1205269-scarred-lands-community-content-frequently-asked-questions?p=1220645#post1220645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a rather silly question about the OGL. For 5E documents, which source must we add in the Copyright Notice. OGL v 1.0a, SRD 5.1 and the PG itself must clearly be there, but I'm not sure about the previous 3E books?</div> </div> </div> </div>The OGL requires you to list all sources of open game content referred to in your books. Since Scarred Lands 5e draws on the Open Game Content from the previous edition, those references are required by the terms of the OGL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T10:38:04-07:00","id":1322059,"title":"","content":"Well, technically, the OGL only applies to game elements, not world elements, as defined in the definition of the product identity... Regardless, I have applied the rule of thumb that you also suggest <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Further question. Let say that I want to include in the description of my new favorite subclass a very small paragraph (one or two sentences max) on how this subclass can be integrated on the other continents of Scarn, and without going too much into the details (foe xample &quot;A number of charduni dwarves from the Empire of Chains on Termana become REDACTED&quot;. Would that be acceptable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Alain%20Giorla\" target=\"_blank\">Slarecian Vault contributions</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5793-haaz","name":"haaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T11:02:38-07:00","id":1322456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1205269-scarred-lands-community-content-frequently-asked-questions?p=1322059#post1322059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, technically, the OGL only applies to game elements, not world elements, as defined in the definition of the product identity... Regardless, I have applied the rule of thumb that you also suggest <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. If you are referencing only setting material, you are fine. But if you are doing any system conversion, I would highly advise you to cite the previous source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1205269-scarred-lands-community-content-frequently-asked-questions?p=1322059#post1322059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further question. Let say that I want to include in the description of my new favorite subclass a very small paragraph (one or two sentences max) on how this subclass can be integrated on the other continents of Scarn, and without going too much into the details (foe xample &quot;A number of charduni dwarves from the Empire of Chains on Termana become REDACTED&quot;. Would that be acceptable?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's honestly a question that should be answered by the community content personnel. I know for the time being, we are keeping things Ghelspad centric, but I think in a case where you feel the FAQ is unclear it would be worthwhile to send an email to the &quot;Email Community Content Help&quot; link in your OBS account page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T03:23:01-07:00","id":1322582,"title":"","content":"The reason I prefer to ask on a public forum is that it can also be useful for people who have the same question<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if you are doing any system conversion, I would highly advise you to cite the previous source. </div> </div> </div>I generally refrain from doing conversions, notably because of this previous answer...It seems noit everyone is following this guideline, and that the moderator team has been pretty relaxed aboiut it until now as far as I can tell, but still...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Can we convert old Scarred Lands OGL material (prestige classes, monsters, spells, magic items, etc) to newer versions of the game (such as 5E or Pathfinder)?</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> The goal of the program is Create. Don't Copy. So, we're mostly interested in new material, especially adventures. So, if updating some of those things makes sense for the new material someone is creating (say you make an adventure that uses an old monster and you want to update that 3e monster to 5e). A straight up compilation of just old stuff to new system isn't actually creating anything, its just copying. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Alain%20Giorla\" target=\"_blank\">Slarecian Vault contributions</a>","edited":{"userid":5793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5793-haaz","user":"haaz","date":". 07-06-2019, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5793-haaz","name":"haaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T10:08:36-07:00","id":1322617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1205269-scarred-lands-community-content-frequently-asked-questions?p=1322582#post1322582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I prefer to ask on a public forum is that it can also be useful for people who have the same question<br /> <br /> I generally refrain from doing conversions, notably because of this previous answer...It seems noit everyone is following this guideline, and that the moderator team has been pretty relaxed aboiut it until now as far as I can tell, but still...<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I understand completely, which is why I refer you (and anyone asking) to the FAQ. The content guidelines there are relatively clear, but (as we all know from sitting around a gaming table) no set of rules is going to address every corner case.<br /> <br /> If a creator legitimately feels their concept is a corner case, reach out.<br /> <br /> If their approach is &quot;how can I skirt the rules?&quot; maybe reevaluate the concept.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T06:54:52-07:00","id":1332809,"title":"","content":"Sorry if it's not the correct place to ask about it, but what is the current status of the setting? Is it on hiatus or are there any plans for continuation and if so, in what terms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-22-2020, 09:25 A